The single biggest mistake a new pilot makes with Jace, Multiverse Architect is putting creature cards into the ninety-nine. Jace's −3 ability exiles a creature or planeswalker you control to reveal cards until hitting a creature or planeswalker card. By running *zero* creature cards in the ninety-nine, every single Jace activation is mathematically guaranteed to hit one of your fifteen Giant Planeswalkers (mana value 5 to 8). Furthermore, if you ever draw a high-cost planeswalker into your hand, do not panic: Jace's +1 allows you to draw two cards and tuck that giant planeswalker directly onto the bottom of your library, perfectly setting up your next −3 activation.

# The Multiverse Architect and the walker cascade
Jace, Multiverse Architect :: Cast for {1}{W}{U}{B}{R}. Taxes opponents {2} to attack your Jaces, draws cards while tucking big walkers with +1, and turns any token into a Giant Planeswalker with −3.
Reality Scramble :: Four-mana sorcery with retrace. Targets any planeswalker or token to reveal until hitting another card sharing that card type, flipping another Giant Planeswalker directly onto the battlefield.
Reweave :: Six-mana instant that sacrifices a permanent to flip into another permanent sharing its card type, turning any planeswalker into another titan.

# The giant planeswalkers
Nicol Bolas, Dragon-God :: Possesses all loyalty abilities of every planeswalker on the battlefield, draws cards, exiles opponent cards, and kills opponents who lack legendary permanents.
Nicol Bolas, God-Pharaoh :: Seven-mana dragon that casts spells for free from opponent libraries, exiles two cards from each opponent's hand, deals 7 damage, or exiles all opponent nonlands.
Nicol Bolas, Planeswalker :: Eight-mana walker that destroys noncreature permanents with +3, steals target creatures with −2, and decimates opponent life and boards with −9.
Ugin, the Spirit Dragon :: Eight-mana colorless powerhouse. Sweeps the entire board of colored permanents with −X while sparing himself, Jace tokens, and your colorless mana rocks.
Ugin, the Ineffable :: Six-mana walker that discounts colorless spells by two, creates 2/2 Spirit tokens that draw cards on death, and destroys target colored permanents.
Elspeth, Sun's Champion :: Six-mana walker that generates three 1/1 Soldier tokens with +1 to fuel repeated Jace −3 activations, or destroys all large creatures with −3.
Elspeth, Storm Slayer :: Doubles all token creation under your control, creating massive swarms of blockers and fodder to feed your planeswalker engine.
Liliana, Dreadhorde General :: Draws cards whenever your tokens or creatures die, creates 2/2 Zombie tokens, and forces each player to sacrifice two creatures with −4.
The Eternal Wanderer :: Restricts opponents to attacking with only one creature per combat, blinks Jace to reset his loyalty counters, and wipes creature boards down to one per player.
Chandra, Awakened Inferno :: Uncounterable six-mana walker that places permanent emblem burn on each opponent each turn and wipes small creatures with −3.
Chandra, Legacy of Fire :: Deals damage to each opponent at your end step equal to the number of planeswalkers you control, and generates red mana for each walker you control.
Teferi, Hero of Dominaria :: Five-mana walker that draws a card and untaps two lands for countermagic, tucks any nonland permanent with −3, and creates an oppressive exile emblem.
Teferi, Temporal Pilgrim :: Draws cards, grows loyalty counters with each draw, generates vigilant Spirit tokens, and shuffles all opponent nonlands away with −12.
Kaya the Inexorable :: Protects your key walkers with ghostform counters, exiles any nonland permanent with −3, and casts free legendary spells every upkeep with −7.
Venser, the Sojourner :: Blinks Jace every turn with +2 to reset his starting loyalty to 4, guaranteeing a −3 Polymorph activation every single turn.
Sarkhan the Masterless :: Punishes attacking creatures with dragon fire, and turns all your planeswalkers into 4/4 flying Dragons for a lethal game-ending aerial assault.

# Token generation and fodder
Bitterblossom :: Two-mana enchantment producing a 1/1 flying Faerie Rogue token every upkeep to provide endless fodder for Jace.
Black Market Connections :: Consistent card draw, Treasure generation, and 3/2 Shapeshifter tokens every upkeep.
Skrelv's Hive :: Two-mana enchantment producing toxic 1/1 Mite tokens every upkeep.
Shark Typhoon :: Cycles at instant speed to create an X/X flying Shark token while replacing itself, setting up an ambush or instant fodder.
Hard Evidence :: One-mana blue sorcery creating an 0/3 Crab token and investigating a Clue token.
Lingering Souls :: Three-mana sorcery producing two 1/1 flying Spirit tokens, with flashback to create two more.
Grand Crescendo :: Scalable instant producing X Citizen tokens while granting your entire board indestructible until end of turn.
Secure the Wastes :: Instant-speed token producer creating X 1/1 Warrior tokens at the end of an opponent's turn.
Sunset Revelry :: Two-mana sorcery that catches you up on life, draws a card, and creates two 1/1 Human tokens.
Jace's Machinations :: Empowers Jace 8 to create an eight-loyalty Jace planeswalker token and allows instant-speed Jace loyalty activations.
Way of the Pyromancer :: Creates a Jace planeswalker token on entry and allows all your planeswalkers to tap for red mana.
Fatehold Charm :: Modal instant that draws a card, empowers Jace 2 to create a Jace token, or bounces a threatening spell or creature.

# Superfriends loyalty doublers and burn engines
Oath of Teferi :: Blinks Jace on entry to reset his loyalty, and allows you to activate the loyalty abilities of each planeswalker you control twice each turn.
The Chain Veil :: Taps for four mana to allow every planeswalker you control to activate an additional loyalty ability that turn.
Ichormoon Gauntlet :: Grants all your planeswalkers a +1 proliferate ability, an extra turn ultimate, and proliferates whenever you cast a noncreature spell.
All Will Be One :: Turns loyalty counters into lethal burn, dealing damage to any target whenever counters are placed on your planeswalkers.
Contagion Engine :: Enters to weaken opponent boards with -1/-1 counters, and proliferates twice for four mana to rapidly accelerate planeswalker ultimates.
Inexorable Tide :: Proliferates on every single spell you cast, quickly advancing your walkers into game-winning ultimates.
Semester's End :: Instant-speed sweeper protection that exiles all your planeswalkers and returns them at end step with additional loyalty counters.
Clever Concealment :: Free convoke instant that phases out all your planeswalkers and permanents in response to removal or board wipes.

# Asymmetric board wipes and countermagic
Urza's Ruinous Blast :: Legendary five-mana sweeper that exiles all nonland permanents that aren't legendary, completely wiping opponents while leaving your planeswalkers untouched.
Supreme Verdict :: Four-mana uncounterable board wipe that clears all creatures without touching your planeswalkers.
Toxic Deluge :: Premier three-mana black sweeper that pays life to bypass indestructible and clear the board.
Blasphemous Act :: Cheap red board wipe costing as little as one red mana on crowded boards.
Damn :: Flexible removal spell casting for two mana to destroy a creature or four mana overloaded to sweep all creatures.
Cyclonic Rift :: Instant-speed asymmetric blowout that bounces all nonland permanents you don't control.
Countersculpt :: Two-mana counterspell that counters any spell and empowers Jace 1 to produce a fresh Jace token.
Dovin's Veto :: Uncounterable two-mana answer to noncreature spells.
Counterspell :: Reliable hard counter for two blue mana.
Swan Song :: Efficient one-mana counter for instant, sorcery, or enchantment spells.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: One-mana noncreature counter.
Mana Drain :: Two-mana counter that converts the countered spell's cost into colorless mana on your next turn.
Anguished Unmaking :: Instant-speed exile for any nonland permanent.
Generous Gift :: Universal spot removal for any problematic permanent.

# Mana acceleration and card draw
Rhystic Study :: Relentless card advantage engine taxing every opponent spell.
Smothering Tithe :: Explosive mana acceleration generating Treasure tokens on opponent card draws.
Sol Ring :: Standard colorless fast mana.
Arcane Signet :: Reliable four-color mana rock.
Fellwar Stone :: Efficient two-mana rock producing pod colors.
Talisman of Progress :: Untapped white and blue mana rock.
Talisman of Dominance :: Untapped blue and black mana rock.
Talisman of Hierarchy :: Untapped white and black mana rock.
Talisman of Creativity :: Untapped blue and red mana rock.
Chromatic Lantern :: Perfect color fixing that turns all your lands into any-color sources.

# Opening hand and sequencing
Prioritize opening hands with 3 lands, at least two colors of early ramp (Sol Ring, Talismans), and a cheap token producer (Bitterblossom, Skrelv's Hive, Hard Evidence, or Jace's Machinations).
On turns 1 through 3, develop your mana rocks and deploy a token generator so a creature or Jace token is already waiting on the battlefield.
On turn 4 or 5, cast Jace, Multiverse Architect and immediately activate his −3 targeting your token, flipping directly into a game-ending Giant Planeswalker.
If you happen to draw a high-mana walker in your hand, activate Jace's +1 to draw two cards and tuck that walker onto the bottom of your library for future Polymorphs.
Once multiple Giant Planeswalkers are deployed, use Oath of Teferi, The Chain Veil, and All Will Be One to double your activations and burn out the table, or activate Sarkhan the Masterless to swing for lethal Dragon damage.
